WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.110 --> 00:00:03.630
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, it's Jan here!

00:00:03.630 --> 00:00:07.680
The super-popular Angry Birds game has been
catapulted on to the big screen to give us

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:08.889
The Angry Birds Movie!

00:00:08.889 --> 00:00:14.309
Cue 97 minutes of bright and breezy colours,
zany action, and briskly-paced comedy, which

00:00:14.309 --> 00:00:17.800
will doubtless keep kids entertained while
providing enough jokes aimed at adults in

00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:19.850
the audience to keep grown-ups happy too.

00:00:19.850 --> 00:00:24.450
The crazy and somewhat slight story revolves
around the avian paradise of Bird Island where

00:00:24.450 --> 00:00:29.430
all the birds are happy, except for Red, who
gets pretty annoyed about everything, including

00:00:29.430 --> 00:00:31.760
the arrival of a bunch of green pigs to the
island.

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:35.400
Now, you don't need to have played the game
before to understand what's going on or to

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:36.400
enjoy the movie.

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:40.350
As you'd probably expect though, whether you're
an Angry Birds addict or a total newcomer,

00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:44.550
there's a stack of bird- and pig-related puns
throughout the film.

00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:50.720
One-liners, sight gags, slapstick, and some
gross-out humour fly by thick and fast, some

00:00:50.720 --> 00:00:51.720
of the jokes hitting, some not.

00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:55.101
There's also quite a number of rather fun
easter eggs and pop culture references and

00:00:55.101 --> 00:00:56.989
I'll have a video on that coming soon.

00:00:56.989 --> 00:01:00.030
I'll add the link here so you can click there
to see it when it's ready!

00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:04.430
The movie's voice cast contains a wealth of
familiar faces hidden behind their animated

00:01:04.430 --> 00:01:06.290
avian and swinish characters.

00:01:06.290 --> 00:01:10.890
Jason Sudeikis, Danny McBride, and Josh Gad
are entertaining as feathered friends Red,

00:01:10.890 --> 00:01:16.000
Bomb and Chuck, who meet at an anger-management
class run by Matilda, who's voiced by Bridesmaids

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:17.550
star Maya Rudolph.

00:01:17.550 --> 00:01:22.479
Sean Penn gets to grunt his way through the
movie as the intimidatingly gruff Terence.

00:01:22.479 --> 00:01:27.180
Inside Out's Bill Hader plays the pig's wickedly
cunning leader Leonard with real glee.

00:01:27.180 --> 00:01:31.390
While Game of Thrones star Peter Dinklage
has an amusing role as the once-heroic Mighty

00:01:31.390 --> 00:01:32.390
Eagle.

00:01:32.390 --> 00:01:36.930
In fact, the voice cast is littered with well-known
names from comedy including Keegan-Michael

00:01:36.930 --> 00:01:42.409
Key, Ike Barinholtz from The Mindy Project,
Veep's Tony Hale, SNL's Kate McKinnon, Tituss

00:01:42.409 --> 00:01:45.409
Burgess from Unbreakable Kimmy Schmidt, and
lots more.

00:01:45.409 --> 00:01:49.780
It's a shame that many of their roles are
so small and that the film flies by so frenetically

00:01:49.780 --> 00:01:53.790
that a number of them don't get to really
register or make a real impact.

00:01:53.790 --> 00:01:57.360
First-time directors Fergal Reilly and Clay
Kaytis and their team of animators have done

00:01:57.360 --> 00:02:01.250
a great job creating incredibly appealing
colourful characters.

00:02:01.250 --> 00:02:05.909
While The Angry Bird Movie doesn't hit the
animated heights of the best of Pixar or Disney,

00:02:05.909 --> 00:02:09.209
or The Lego Movie, say, it's still a good
deal of fun.

00:02:09.209 --> 00:02:14.210
So, to sum up: The Angry Birds Movie is lively,
entertaining, and bursting at the seams with

00:02:14.210 --> 00:02:18.060
quality voice cast, anarchic attitude, and
a barrage of jokes.

00:02:18.060 --> 00:02:22.110
While it's not the animated equivalent of
a gourmet meal to be lingered over, it's certainly

00:02:22.110 --> 00:02:24.150
a tasty fast-food treat.

00:02:24.150 --> 00:02:27.349
The Angry Birds Movie gets 3 out of 5 Flicks.

00:02:27.349 --> 00:02:29.690
Now, what did you think of The Angry Birds
Movie?

00:02:29.690 --> 00:02:32.900
And if you've played the Angry Birds game,
did you like the way they adapted it for the

00:02:32.900 --> 00:02:33.900
big screen?

